   "answer": "The provided lecture material does not contain any information about a user named \"yuxinye,\" their specific TACC job, or any real-time GPU utilization metrics.\n\nThe available evidence only discusses general concepts of GPU parallelism and SIMD utilization:\n*   [S1] (Page 33) defines parallelism, data parallelism, and task parallelism.\n*   [S3] (Page 46) discusses optimizing GPU throughput and SIMD utilization by controlling divergence in code.\n*   [S2] (Page 67) mentions that \"real ceilings fall with poor locality or pipeline utilization,\" but provides no specific data or calculations for any individual job.\n\nTherefore, it is impossible to determine the real-time GPU utilization of yuxinye's current TACC job using only the currently imported lecture.",
